{
  "_what": "What a person's own API accounts cost them, counted where Trillion sends to them (src/api-spend.mjs, through the one send every connected service's request passes: src/workshop.mjs sendThroughBox). services are the connections whose answers say what they used: { connection_id, label, prices: [{ model, per_million: { measure: dollars }, above?: { input_tokens, per_million } }], source }. A call's model is read from its request body, else its answer (model_at); its usage from the answer (usage paths, one list of paths per measure, the first that holds a number wins); output is never less than total minus input, so thinking a service reports only in its total is still counted. A model's price is the row whose model is the longest start of the call's model; above prices every token of a call whose input passed that many tokens. A call with no price row is counted as calls and tokens with its dollars unknown, never as free. Cached input is priced as plain input, so dollars are never below the bill. Prices are hand-typed from each service's own page on read_on; a service, a model or a price is a row here.",
